<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2012/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>Comentality.Events2Code</id>
    <version>1.1.0</version>
    <title>Events2Code</title>
    <authors>Comentality</authors>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://comentality.com/tools/#events2code</projectUrl>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/comentality/xrm-events-2-code.git" branch="main" />
    <icon>icon.png</icon>
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
    <description>Convert Dynamics 365 form event handler registrations made in the form designer UI into equivalent JavaScript code, and unregister them from the form.</description>
    <releaseNotes>v1.1.0
- Changing the connection now clears the old environment from the window, so no write can land in the wrong one.
- On a slow connection the forms list and handler grid always show what you clicked last, and the buttons wait for it.
- Loading tables, forms and a form's XML can now be cancelled from the Cancel button on the loading panel.
- A failed load now stays on the status line, which also says what is still loading instead of counting too early.
- Closing the tab mid-load no longer pops up an error later, and a save to a dead share no longer freezes the window.
Full changelog, with screenshots: https://github.com/comentality/xrm-events-2-code/releases/tag/v1.1.0

v1.0.0
- Browse tables and their Main and Quick Create forms over an XrmToolBox connection, with a filter on display or logical name.
- List every event handler a form registers through the designer, with its event, target, function, library and enabled state.
- Generate a single OnLoad bootstrap function that registers the checked handlers through the Client API.
- Designer quirks are preserved: extra parameters and the "pass execution context" flag are re-emitted through wrapper closures.
- Copy the generated code to the clipboard or save it to a .js file.
- Unregister the checked handlers: they leave the form XML, the bootstrap is registered on form OnLoad, and the table is published.
- Back up the form XML to Documents\Events2Code\backups before any change, and warn on managed forms.
- The generated-code preview is syntax highlighted.
</releaseNotes>
    <tags>XrmToolBox Dynamics365 CRM PowerPlatform JavaScript FormEvents</tags>
    <dependencies>
      <group targetFramework=".NETFramework4.8">
        <dependency id="XrmToolBox" version="1.2025.7.71" />
      </group>
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="bin\Release\net48\Events2Code.dll" target="Plugins\Events2Code.dll" />
    <file src="icon.png" target="icon.png" />
    <file src="..\README.md" target="docs\README.md" />
  </files>
</package>
